Subject: Preservation Notice for Pending Product Liability Claim

Dear [General Counsel Name],

I am writing to confirm that Meridian BioPharma must preserve all documents and electronically stored information (“ESI”) that may relate to the pending product liability claim. This includes materials that could be relevant to the product at issue, its design, testing, manufacturing, quality control, labeling, distribution, complaints, adverse event reports, investigations, communications, and any potential defenses or damages.

Please ensure that a litigation hold is issued promptly and that routine deletion, overwriting, auto-purge functions, and other document destruction practices are suspended for potentially relevant custodians and systems. Preservation should extend to both hard-copy and electronic materials, including emails, text messages, instant messages, shared drives, cloud-based files, databases, and backup media to the extent reasonably necessary.

Examples of materials to preserve include:
- internal and external communications concerning the product or claim;
- batch records, specifications, SOPs, test data, and quality records;
- complaint files, adverse event reports, recalls, and CAPA materials;
- regulatory submissions and correspondence;
- documents reflecting sales, distribution, and customer contacts;
- calendars, notes, and drafts relating to the claim.

Please confirm that key employees, relevant custodians, and IT personnel have been notified of the hold and instructed to preserve potentially relevant information. If helpful, we can assist with identifying custodians and drafting the hold notice.

Best regards,  
[Your Name]  
Outside Counsel

Certainly — below is a lender-friendly, checklist-style **Conditions Precedent to Initial Borrowing** clause drafted for a syndicated credit agreement. You can adapt defined terms and bracketed items to fit the rest of the agreement.

---

## Section [●]. Conditions Precedent to Initial Borrowing

**The obligation of each Lender to make the Initial Borrowing shall be subject to the satisfaction, prior to or substantially concurrently with such Initial Borrowing, of each of the following conditions precedent, each in form and substance satisfactory to the Administrative Agent and the Required Lenders:**

### (a) Execution and Delivery of Credit Documents
The Administrative Agent shall have received each of the following, duly executed and delivered by each Loan Party, as applicable:

1. this Agreement;
2. the Notes, if any, requested by any Lender;
3. the Guaranty, if any;
4. the Security Agreement and each other Collateral Document required to be executed on or prior to the Initial Borrowing Date;
5. each fee letter, intercreditor agreement, subordination agreement, joinder agreement, and other document contemplated by the Loan Documents to be delivered at or prior to the Initial Borrowing; and
6. all other Loan Documents required to be executed and delivered on or before the Initial Borrowing Date.

### (b) Organizational Documents; Resolutions; Incumbency
The Administrative Agent shall have received, in each case certified as true, correct and complete as of a recent date reasonably satisfactory to the Administrative Agent:

1. copies of the certificate or articles of incorporation, formation, organization or equivalent organizational documents of each Loan Party;
2. copies of the by-laws, operating agreement, partnership agreement or other governing documents of each Loan Party;
3. certificates of good standing, existence or equivalent status for each Loan Party from its jurisdiction of organization and, to the extent reasonably requested, each jurisdiction in which the failure to so qualify could reasonably be expected to have a Material Adverse Effect;
4. resolutions, consents or other authorizing actions of the board of directors, managers, members, partners or other governing body of each Loan Party authorizing the execution, delivery and performance of the Loan Documents and the Transactions;
5. an incumbency certificate of each Loan Party, setting forth the names and signatures of the officers or other authorized persons executing the Loan Documents and any certificates delivered in connection therewith; and
6. specimen signatures of the persons authorized to execute such documents, if requested by the Administrative Agent.

