- Whether Ellis engaged in protected activity and, if so, whether there is a causal connection to the termination or other adverse action;
- Whether Ellis worked overtime hours for which compensation was not paid, and whether the defendant had actual or constructive knowledge of those hours;
- Whether the defendant’s payroll, scheduling, and supervisory practices support or undermine the overtime allegations.

